<https://purl.eu/ns/mobility/passenger-transport-hubs> a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Ontology>.
<https://purl.eu/ns/mobility/passenger-transport-hubs#TransportHub> a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://purl.eu/ns/mobility/passenger-transport-hubs>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Place where passengers and/or freight are exchanged between vehicles and/or modes of transport."@en;
    <http://purl.org/vocab/vann/usageNote> "Examples for passenger transport are train stations, underground stations, bus stations, airports, ferry terminals, car parks... For freight transport it concerns typically airports, seaports, transhipment terminals. Transport hubs are typically intermodal, for example travellers combine the (shared) bicycle with the train for their trip, but intramodal transfers (for example from one bus line to another) are also important. Concretely, a Transport hub includes infrastructure (stations, car parks, charging infrastructure... ), (mobility) services (public transport lines, shared bicycles, shops... ) and nodes in transport networks (public transport stops, car sharing points... )."@en;
    <http://www.w3.org/ns/adms#status> <https://data.vlaanderen.be/id/concept/StandaardStatus/ErkendeStandaard>.
<https://purl.eu/ns/mobility/passenger-transport-hubs#InformationCarrier> a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://purl.eu/ns/mobility/passenger-transport-hubs>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Panel or board or similar infrastructure on which information is displayed."@en;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://data.vlaanderen.be/ns/openbaardomein/infrastructuur#Infrastructuurelement>;
    <http://purl.org/vocab/vann/usageNote> "Intended as a means of communication, usually used in public spaces to inform passers-by. Both static carriers such as information boards with a city map and dynamic systems with for example public transport departure times are possible."@en;
    <http://www.w3.org/ns/adms#status> <https://data.vlaanderen.be/id/concept/StandaardStatus/ErkendeStandaard>.
<https://purl.eu/ns/mobility/passenger-transport-hubs#DataExchangeInfrastructure> a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://purl.eu/ns/mobility/passenger-transport-hubs>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Physical facilities aimed at exchanging data."@en;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://data.vlaanderen.be/ns/openbaardomein/infrastructuur#Infrastructuurelement>;
    <http://purl.org/vocab/vann/usageNote> "For example servers, cables, modems."@en;
    <http://www.w3.org/ns/adms#status> <https://data.vlaanderen.be/id/concept/StandaardStatus/ErkendeStandaard>.
<https://purl.eu/ns/mobility/passenger-transport-hubs#Hoppinpoint> a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://purl.eu/ns/mobility/passenger-transport-hubs>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Transport hub of the mobility brand Hoppin."@en;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://purl.eu/ns/mobility/passenger-transport-hubs#RegisteredTransportHub>;
    <http://purl.org/vocab/vann/usageNote> "Hoppin is the name under which the Flemish government indicates transport hubs for passenger transport that meet fixed (quality) requirements. Important aspects are recognisability (application of the Hoppin house style), accessibility (for all users irrespective of disability, age, etc.), minimum equipment (for example bicycle sheds, information supports, etc.), alignment with mobility plans, etc."@en;
    <http://www.w3.org/ns/adms#status> <https://data.vlaanderen.be/id/concept/StandaardStatus/ErkendeStandaard>.
<https://purl.eu/ns/mobility/passenger-transport-hubs#RegisteredTransportHub> a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://purl.eu/ns/mobility/passenger-transport-hubs>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Passenger Transport Hub recognised as such."@en;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://purl.eu/ns/mobility/passenger-transport-hubs#TransportHub>;
    <http://purl.org/vocab/vann/usageNote> "This recognition implies that a Registered Transport Hub is formally designated as a Transport Hub. Typically, this is done by the government to give the hub an official character (recognisable for the user, meets imposed quality requirements...)."@en;
    <http://www.w3.org/ns/adms#status> <https://data.vlaanderen.be/id/concept/StandaardStatus/ErkendeStandaard>.
<https://purl.eu/ns/mobility/passenger-transport-hubs#Charger> a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://purl.eu/ns/mobility/passenger-transport-hubs>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An object that provides electrical energy for charging electric vehicles."@en;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://data.vlaanderen.be/ns/openbaardomein/infrastructuur#Infrastructuurelement>, <https://schema.org/CivicStructure>;
    <http://www.w3.org/ns/adms#status> <https://data.vlaanderen.be/id/concept/StandaardStatus/ErkendeStandaard>.
<https://purl.eu/ns/mobility/passenger-transport-hubs#AdditionalService> a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://purl.eu/ns/mobility/passenger-transport-hubs>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Service that complements or supports other Services."@en;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://purl.eu/ns/mobility/transporthubs#Service>;
    <http://purl.org/vocab/vann/usageNote> "For example Newspaper shop, Postal service or Restaurant in a Station. Services that are supplemented or supported by this are for example Mobility Services."@en;
    <http://www.w3.org/ns/adms#status> <https://data.vlaanderen.be/id/concept/StandaardStatus/ErkendeStandaard>.
<https://purl.eu/ns/mobility/passenger-transport-hubs#VirtualNode> a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://purl.eu/ns/mobility/passenger-transport-hubs>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Transport node that is dynamically created."@en;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://data.vlaanderen.be/ns/transportnetwerk#Transportknoop>;
    <http://purl.org/vocab/vann/usageNote> "The place where a Trip is started usually does not coincide with an existing Transport node, for example it is the home of the Traveller located between two intersections. To still enter the network to start his Trip, the Traveller creates a Virtual Node on the link between these intersections. Virtual Nodes are important for a correct estimation of the travel time for example for route planning because the distance between the Virtual Node and the next real Transport Node must be added. Also important for example in free-floating partial transport where the position of the partial step does not necessarily coincide with that of an existing Transport Node."@en;
    <http://www.w3.org/ns/adms#status> <https://data.vlaanderen.be/id/concept/StandaardStatus/ErkendeStandaard>.
<https://purl.eu/ns/mobility/passenger-transport-hubs#HoppinColumn> a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://purl.eu/ns/mobility/passenger-transport-hubs>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Information column of a Hoppinpoint."@en;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://data.vlaanderen.be/doc/applicatieprofiel/infrastructuurelementen/#Infozuil>;
    <http://purl.org/vocab/vann/usageNote> "Intended to indicate that a Transport hub is a Hoppin point and/or to inform about the transport possibilities offered there.\nMore info can be found in the implementation model: https://wegenenverkeer.data.vlaanderen.be/doc/implementatiemodel/hoppinpunten/."@en;
    <http://www.w3.org/ns/adms#status> <https://data.vlaanderen.be/id/concept/StandaardStatus/ErkendeStandaard>.
<https://purl.eu/ns/mobility/passenger-transport-hubs#TransportRegion> a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://purl.eu/ns/mobility/passenger-transport-hubs>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Clusters of municipalities in which mobility is coordinated."@en;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/Location>;
    <http://www.w3.org/ns/adms#status> <https://data.vlaanderen.be/id/concept/StandaardStatus/ErkendeStandaard>.
<https://purl.eu/ns/mobility/passenger-transport-hubs#ResourceReport> a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://purl.eu/ns/mobility/passenger-transport-hubs>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Report of how many Resources with similar characteristics of availability, type, service, location etc are present at a certain point in time."@en;
    <http://purl.org/vocab/vann/usageNote> "For example The number of available bikes in a particular train station."@en;
    <http://www.w3.org/ns/adms#status> <https://data.vlaanderen.be/id/concept/StandaardStatus/ErkendeStandaard>.
<https://purl.eu/ns/mobility/passenger-transport-hubs#number> a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://purl.eu/ns/mobility/passenger-transport-hubs>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://purl.eu/ns/mobility/passenger-transport-hubs#ResourceReport>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The number of resources."@en;
    <http://www.w3.org/ns/adms#status> <https://data.vlaanderen.be/id/concept/StandaardStatus/ErkendeStandaard>.
<https://purl.eu/ns/mobility/passenger-transport-hubs#TransportHub.classification> a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://purl.eu/ns/mobility/passenger-transport-hubs>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://purl.eu/ns/mobility/passenger-transport-hubs#TransportHub>;
